<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Armistice of 11 November 1918</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as armistice · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Armistice of 11 November 1918 was the agreement that ended fighting on the Western Front between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. It was signed after Germany's military position collapsed and revolution broke out at home. It coincided with the abdication of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-ii">Wilhelm II</a> and the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918.jpg" alt="Armistice of 11 November 1918" width="314" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Armisticetrain_(slight_crop).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
